[2] {"source_title": "Thomas Fearnley", "temporal_status": "unknown"}
. He was a student of the Norwegian National Academy of Craft and Art Industry ( Den kongelige Tegneskole ) ( 1819–1821 ) , Art Academy ( Kunstakadamie ) in Copenhagen ( 1821–1823 ) and the Art Academy ( Konstakadamien ) in Stockholm ( 1823–27 ) under .

