The painting survived the fire in the Alcazar which destroyed some of the Spanish royal collection , and by 1794 had been moved to the Palacio Nuevo , the present Royal Palace of Madrid . In 1816 the painting was in London , in the possession of Colonel James Hay , a Scottish soldier . He claimed that after he was seriously wounded at the Battle of Waterloo the previous year , the painting hung in the room where he convalesced in Brussels . He fell in love with it , and persuaded the owner to sell . More relevant to the real facts is no doubt Hays presence at the Battle of Vitoria ( 1813 ) in Spain , where a large coach loaded by King Joseph Bonaparte with easily portable artworks from the royal collections was first plundered by British troops , before what was left was recovered by their commanders and returned to the Spanish .

